{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384304-personal-take-on-technocracy-and-their-paradigm","id":1384304,"title":"Personal take on Technocracy and their Paradigm","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-27T17:18:47-07:00","id":1384304,"title":"Personal take on Technocracy and their Paradigm","content":"Hi. Im not sure if this topic has been around here before (probably; thanks in advance if you can re-direct me to the thread) <br /> <br /> The more I read about it, the less I understand how is possible that most technocrats dont realize what they do is altering reality right away (magic), specially when they clearly use terms as &quot;Consensual Reality&quot; or &quot;Reality Deviant&quot;. Since the aforementioned situation doesnt make sense to me, I've been thinking about using the following approach in my chronicle:<br /> <br /> &quot;We know reality can be bent and modified through several paradigms. Thats what reality deviants do. Thing is, all of them are TOO DANGEROUS. All of them betray what the masses want (Consensual Reality). All of them must be exterminated. All of them but ours, the only one which is actually SAFE&quot;.<br /> <br /> In other words, making most of the &quot;Enlightened&quot; personnel (or at least those above Arete 2) aware of what they are, what they do, but specially, WHY THEY DO IT THE WAY THEY DO IT. Has anyone tried a similar approach? What implications would that have?<br /> <br /> Honestly, it's hard for me to buy something like: &quot;Oh, that deviant is flying thanks to some scientific principle we do not understand yet, but she's just...singing a song (or whatever non-scientific focus that mage is using)&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:16:28-07:00","id":1384318,"title":"","content":"That's always been a tough thing to figure out or justify but I try to look at it this way: prior to scientific study, all manner of things were considered &quot;magic&quot;. A lot of this was hogwash but some of it were actual scientific principles that people just didn't understand. <br /> <br /> Vikings using a magic sun rock to navigate the oceans was actually taking advantage of the use of the properties of cordierite. <br /> <br /> Lighting a fire almost instantly with a small magical wooden stick and tube was the use of a fire piston<br /> <br /> Chinese dragon bones were actually dinosaur bones<br /> <br /> Magic death rocks were things like torbernite<br /> <br /> The walls of Jericho could have fallen due to mechanical resonance<br /> <br /> Now imagine if you were an actual scientist and saw all sorts of people following completely unscientific principles and no safety procedures while trying dangerous stuff like: trying to induce the placebo effect by feeding people a mix of dinosaur bones and Mercury; hypnotizing people with a mix of hypnosis techniques and poisonous chemical substances to gain their worship and money; mixing powerful explosives powders and liquids to try and make fireworks while in a crowded apartment building; using a lightning rod to sacrifice a person to the lightning gods, or tossing people into a deep pit of radioactive material for good luck.<br /> <br /> You'd be upset, I reckon. You know things don't work quite how these idiots imagine and that they are a danger to themselves and others. Now dial that up to a hundred and you get a Technocrat looking at reality deviants taking bits of poorly understood or thoroughly misunderstood hypertech principles and using it in ways that endanger themselves, others, and the very fabric of reality, which the Technocracy is desperately trying to make safe for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-27-2020, 09:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:20:45-07:00","id":1384319,"title":"","content":"My preferred approach is very similar to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5394_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5394\" data-vbnamecard=\"5394\">Argonot</a>'s; the only thing I do differently is that the Technocrats in my game say \u201cthat Reality-bending stuff is something the Reality Deviants do; but it's not what <i>we</i> do: the Enlightened Science that <i>we</i> engage in builds on solid Earthly Foundations and thus is more natural and elegant \u2014 and, yes, ultimately safer \u2014 than what the Superstitionists peddle.\u201d <br /> <br /> The Traditions say that it's all just Willworking; but they may be <i>wrong</i> about that. And the Technocrats say that there's a fundamental difference between what they do and what the mages do; and they may be <i>right</i> about that. Or the mages may be right and the Technocrats wrong. <br /> <br /> The key point is that unless you invoke authorial intent, there's no way to <i>know</i>: there's nothing in the setting itself that conclusively dictates that one side is fundamentally right and the other fundamentally wrong. It rather, there's evidence on both sides: the Traditions have the fact that an Enlightened Scientist can turn over a new leaf and become a High Ritualist or even a Chaos Magician and vice versa (though that's highly unlikely without outside intervention), and the Technocracy has the fact that there are things Traditions can do that Technocrats can't and vice versa (Surpassing your Focus on the one hand; accessing Primal Ventures and setting up assembly lines for Devices on the other). <br /> <br /> I'll revisit this over the coming weeks to see if <b>Technocracy Reloaded</b> changes my mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:44:41-07:00","id":1384327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384304-personal-take-on-technocracy-and-their-paradigm#post1384304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, that deviant is flying thanks to some scientific principle we do not understand yet, but she's just...singing a song (or whatever non-scientific focus that mage is using)&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking it would be more like: I reckon she's found a way to use her bioelectromagnetic field as a magnetoaerodynamic drive... Like a magnetohydrodynamic drive, but in air. Who knows what harm she's doing to her body. She could probably accidentally fry her brain doing that. Maybe some extradimensional being modified her physiology and there's some truth to that angel thing she mentioned. No, I don't know why she's singing.<br /> <br /> (I see nothing wrong with your approach though.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12480,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","user":"Spacecat","date":". 04-28-2020, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T07:41:27-07:00","id":1384408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384304-personal-take-on-technocracy-and-their-paradigm?p=1384319#post1384319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My preferred approach is very similar to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5394_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5394\" data-vbnamecard=\"5394\">Argonot</a>'s; the only thing I do differently is that the Technocrats in my game say \u201cthat Reality-bending stuff is something the Reality Deviants do; but it's not what <i>we</i> do: the Enlightened Science that <i>we</i> engage in builds on solid Earthly Foundations and thus is more natural and elegant \u2014 and, yes, ultimately safer \u2014 than what the Superstitionists peddle.\u201d<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>So, the technocrats in your game are aware Reality CAN be bent over. They know deviants can unweave/reweave it somehow. I ask because, if I understand what the books actually say, most technocrats (but the high spheres) reject that idea right away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T09:41:20-07:00","id":1384433,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Technocrats in my game (mostly) are aware that reality can be changed through Willworking. The exceptions are typically in some stage of Denial, with the most extreme of them crossing the line into the Negation Men phenomenon. <br /> <br /> There are enough who are in Denial that it's a known problem for the Union; but it's a significant minority, not a majority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-28T13:50:48-07:00","id":1384494,"title":"","content":"Rather than a personal take, here's an excerpt from the first part of Technocracy Reloaded, explaining their view of the matter:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Reality, as we know it, is formed by the collective belief of humanity. Billions of people define the boundaries of Consensual Reality; the world you see around you on Earth is the world mankind wants. Seven billion people look up at the sky each day and know it should be blue (even when it\u2019s a little gray and rainy). Seven billion people instinctively know that gravity works. The parameters of our universe are consistent with conditions for life as we know it the universe sentient humans observe and inhabit \u2014 and, according to Anthropic Field Theory, human consciousness directs the flow of Earthly phenomena. Consensual Reality is the reason for everything we see and experience around us.<br /> <br /> In the world of our Union, we know this is true because we have seen people who want an alternative: individuals who defy and deviate from this Consensus. Reality Deviants rework and reshape the world around themselves through sheer force of will, for better or for worse. When all things are possible, whenever one person defies the collective belief of over seven billion people, it\u2019s usually for the worse. If one person who believes that magic is real summons a dragon in the heart of Manhattan, you know what happens next: Nothing good. Both humanity and reality actively resist that deviant act. That\u2019s why the Paradox Effect exists.<br /> <br /> :<br /> <br /> \u201cMagick,\u201d as they refer to it, is, in its most potent form, one of the greatest threats to human existence. Defying reality, one individual can do the impossible. That defiance carries a risk: reality can strike back. Witnesses accumulate. Paradoxes manifest. Belief itself is challenged. Humans remain asleep and dreaming of a world where magic does not exist, but when those sleepers awaken, innocent citizens get hurt. While the Masses find the fictional forms of \u201cmovie magic\u201d entertaining, and while they may serve as acceptable and profitable safety valve for oblivious minds, true Reality Deviance is dangerous. Thus, it must be suppressed, controlled, converted or, in some cases, destroyed.<br /> <br /> :<br /> <br /> Fortunately, we have our own strengths: Unity, purpose, galvanizing ideals, a sense of responsibility, and technology that\u2019s decades ahead of what the rest of humanity possesses. When we act, we don\u2019t turn back the clock. The more we use our Enlightened technology, the more powerful and possible our technology becomes. Eventually, what we envision and create will be accessible by all of humanity. Ordinary men and women then become masters of their own world while our Union continues to march towards tomorrow. We\u2019re always innovating our advanced technology, and we\u2019re leading the way to the future. </div> </div> </div>This is followed by a \u201cDisputed Data\u201d box that addresses the issue from a more neutral perspective, and is also well worth reading. It doesn't go as far as I would; but I expected that. Still, it's a heck of a lot closer to my approach than to the \u201cmagic isn't real\u201d stereotype that many have of the Union's views.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T02:55:59-07:00","id":1384606,"title":"","content":"Here's my personal take on how the technocracy deals with the contradiction.<br /> There's only so much cognitive dissonance a person can take before they finally have to accept the evidence in front of their eyes. The technocracy operatives that regularly deal with reality deviants, extradimensional entities and other super...sorry, I mean unexplained phenomena will sooner or later start asking questions. That's when someone from management calls them to have &quot;the talk&quot;. The pitch is basically this: Yes, there are other ways but ours is the right one. Why you ask? Simple, everybody can use a phone but only a few can summon a spirit wind to carry a message...oh, and using the phone doesn't require you sacrificing a small animal to work.<br /> What I mean with this is that technology is for everyone, sure the technocracy has committed, and it's still committing, many mistakes, and technology has been used to bring a lot of suffering, but you can't argue that when you put the good and the bad in a balance the good outweighs the bad. Now let's look at the traditions on the other hand, their Magick is elitist by design and only a few can use it. Also, I don't see the traditions trying to make their ways readily available for the masses, quite the opposite in fact. As far as I know, the technocracy are the only ones who have actively tried to make their paradigm available for everyone (for the most part). <br /> So yes, in my game technocrats with arete 3 or higher know that there are other ways, but they also know that their way is the right way, the one that will ultimately empower the people even if they don't always get it right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T07:06:21-07:00","id":1384647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Throughout our world in the 21st century, the Technocratic vision of reality holds the coincidental edge, not simply because of the Union's indoctrination (although that <i>does</i> have something to do with it) but because science-based technology is rooted in following the laws of Earthly physics. Unlike faith and magic, it's based upon repeatable, verifiable, consistent results, not mere Enlightened Will, so it tends to work more reliably than mystic magic does.<br /> <br /> <b>M20</b> p.613 </div> </div> </div>Between that and the section on Earthly Foundations just prior to it, it's clear that even in the world of Mage, there <i>is</i> a \u201cbaseline reality\u201d; and things that build on that foundation tend to fare better than things that deviate from it. <br /> <br /> As of TR, I'm not even sure that there's an initial period of Enlightenment 1 and 2 where a Technocrat doesn't believe in magic. I think that Firanai's \u201cthe talk\u201d is part of standard initiation into the Union, and that the party line isn't that magic isn't real, but rather than it's unreliable. \u201cOurs isn't the only way, but it's the best way\u201d isn't some secret that gets presented to more advanced agents; it's part of the Union's basic training. <br /> <br /> I've heard that TR is going to delve into something called \u201cterranorming\u201d; and from how I've heard the term used, it has something to do with shifting Reality Zones toward the Technocratic ones \u2014 the ones that were described in the quote at the beginning of this post. I'm very interested in seeing what that turns out to be like, as that may very well be one of the \u201csecret weapons\u201d that the Union has in the Ascension War. Note that the initial quote here <i>didn't</i> come from a section presented from the Technocracy's perspective; there <i>really is</i> a coincidental edge held by the Technocratic vision of reality, and that comes at least in part from the Union promoting science and technology instead of leaning into Willworking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T09:55:04-07:00","id":1384660,"title":"","content":"My personal impression from revised was that most technocrats knew that reality was mutable to some degree but that they always considered themselves to be the ones who knew the exact principles involved and that they thought of magic users as something like cultist trying to make atomic weapons with half understood notes and lots of trial and error.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12480-spacecat","name":"Spacecat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"597"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T11:53:45-07:00","id":1384676,"title":"","content":"Thanks for that text Dataweaver, I forgot it was there.<br /> <br /> Let me elaborate my personal take on the technocracy and Magick. Here's the thing, my technocracy doesn't negate the existence of &quot;Magick&quot; to new operatives (Arete 1 and 2), they just explain differently. After all you can't just hope that the young agent will ignore how a reality deviant just conjured a fireball out of thin air in his first mission. So, in the end they (ironically) do what every other mage group does: <b>Explain it through the lens of their paradigm.</b><br /> <br /> As such, the official posture of the Technocratic Union (in my games) regarding reality deviants is that they are NOT mages, or do so called &quot;Magick&quot;, their deviant abilities come from either one or a combination of the sourcesbellow<b> whose origin <b>th</b>ey wrongly attribute to retrograde and superstitious paradigms,</b>and of course they can all be explained by science:<ul><li>They make pacts with dangerous aliens and extradimensional beings.</li> <li>They are individuals with strong noetic (psychic) skills.</li> <li>They are I.A.G. (Individuals with anomalous genetics or mutants)</li> <li>They are using hypertech and exotic materials to create powerful but unstable devices, implants and drugs.</li> </ul>When an agent has accumulated enough experience (Reached Arete 3) is when management gives them &quot;the talk&quot; where they explain that, yes, reality is a bit more complex, and flexible, than what they thought and, from a certain point of view, technocrats do share certain similarities with the reality deviants.<br /> <b>However, that's not the point. </b><br /> The point is that after everything the agent has seen, it should be more than clear to them that, yes, the technocratic way it's not the only way, <b>but it's definitively the ONLY GOOD WAY.</b><br /> The ultimate objective from management is not to confuse younger operatives and let them see for themselves a truth that the masters know is self-evident: the Technocratic Union paradigm is the best for humanity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2964,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","user":"Firanai","date":". 04-29-2020, 03:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2964-firanai","name":"Firanai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2964_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-29T12:08:41-07:00","id":1384679,"title":"","content":"Another relevant excerpt: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the Technocracy is concerned, Union operatives do not use \u201cmagick\u201d and are not \u201cmages\u201d of any kind. That perspective involves a fair amount of cognitive dissonance, and a few early Mage books suggest that Technocrats are simply mages deliberately fooling Sleepers into believing that what they do is not magick. Officially, however, the Union does not recognize \u2014 ever \u2014 that Enlightened technology is a variation of what other mages do. Syndicate agents might be able to get away with throwing the M-word around in a snide, ironic fashion (and may privately admit that money is essentially an act of magick with that will-working \u201ck\u201d attached at the end), but the Technocratic party line is that Enlightened Science differs radically from \u201cmagic.\u201d Magic(k)al powers are Deviant; Enlightened Science is technology, and any good Technocrat draws a bold distinction between the two.<br /> <br /> That said, the Union does recognize that their procedures hold the same realityaltering qualities that magick does, and that their science is subject to the Paradox Effect. Likewise, they realize that mages can be Socially Processed into discarding magick in favor of Enlightened Science, and that the most effective applications of that Science do require Enlightenment / Awakening. A heretical few even dare to look back at the accomplishments of their illustrious predecessors in the Order of Reason and admit that what those forebears were doing was essentially \u201cmagick,\u201d too. Never will that acknowledgement, however, be made in a public or official capacity. Maintaining a distinction between Enlightened Science and Deviant \u201cmagick\u201d is essential to the Technocratic mindset \u2014 which, in game terms, is one reason why Technocratic characters cannot outgrow their need for a technological focus (Mage 20, pp. 329 and 567). </div> </div> </div>So the main divide between the Traditions and the Technocracy isn't that they both say that they're all doing the same thing but differ on what that thing is. No, the main divide is that the Traditions are saying that it's all Magick while the Technocracy says that Enlightened Science and the deviant arts are two different, albeit similar, things. <br /> <br /> And frankly, the Technocracy isn't even all that unique in that regard. The notion that it's ultimately all the same thing is an innovation of the Traditions, and is the glue that holds them together. But outside of the Traditions, \u201cWe Are All Gods in Disguise\u201d may not even be a majority-held Paradigm let alone a universal one. What TR is saying in that regard is that WAGID is <i>anathema</i> to the Technocracy's beliefs, and you will not find a Technocrat with that Paradigm in his Focus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T20:39:12-07:00","id":1384994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384304-personal-take-on-technocracy-and-their-paradigm?p=1384494#post1384494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rather than a personal take, here's an excerpt from the first part of Technocracy Reloaded, explaining their view of the matter:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This is followed by a \u201cDisputed Data\u201d box that addresses the issue from a more neutral perspective, and is also well worth reading. It doesn't go as far as I would; but I expected that. Still, it's a heck of a lot closer to my approach than to the \u201cmagic isn't real\u201d stereotype that many have of the Union's views.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wow, I didnt know some material from TR was available already. Thank you so much. I think that text it's exactly what I needed.<br /> <br /> I'm glad they're moving Technocracy into that direction, which, from a personal point of view, makes much more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5394-argonot","name":"Argonot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5394_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T21:15:03-07:00","id":1384997,"title":"","content":"Mind you, there's nothing stopping technocrats from merging themselves with their tools. Sure, a Master techno merged with a nanobot hive or a gravitic disruptor (to imitate telekinesis) is still bound to the need for technology as a focus, but to the poor saps on the receiving end, the difference is academic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:24:02-07:00","id":1385007,"title":"","content":"Yeah; the Kickstarters have been releasing chapters weekly from the 99% finished manuscript for at least the last half-dozen of them. This week was the Introduction and Unit 1; next week I expect will be at least Units 2 and 3, possibly even 4 (though probably not). There are nine sections to the manuscript (the Introduction and 8 Units) and they're being released over a four-week period, so that's seven Units over the remaining three weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:29:30-07:00","id":1385009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384304-personal-take-on-technocracy-and-their-paradigm?p=1384997#post1384997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you, there's nothing stopping technocrats from merging themselves with their tools. Sure, a Master techno merged with a nanobot hive or a gravitic disruptor (to imitate telekinesis) is still bound to the need for technology as a focus, but to the poor saps on the receiving end, the difference is academic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, that all depends on what your tools are. I can see some in ItX going full borg and some Progenitors upgrading themselves to Transhuman status; but the NWO, Syndicate, and Could Engineers are generally less likely to \u201cbecome one with\u201d their tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T22:39:11-07:00","id":1385010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1384304-personal-take-on-technocracy-and-their-paradigm?p=1385009#post1385009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, that all depends on what your tools are. I can see some in ItX going full borg and some Progenitors upgrading themselves to Transhuman status; but the NWO, Syndicate, and Could Engineers are generally less likely to \u201cbecome one with\u201d their tools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Void Engineers become The Doctor. The other two? Its obvious they use techniques comboed with tech. NWO can walk down the street and cause entire nations to fall in line with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}